{{Quote|When I was a little girl&hellip; pirates captured me. They sold me to a Hutt clan. I&hellip; worked as a slave for years until I finally escaped.|Nenavakasa Nalor, to Neeku Vozo|<ref name="The Engineer" />}}
'''Kintan''' was a [[planet]]<ref name="Nikto (Red)" /> located in the [[Kintan system]] within [[Hutt Space]] in grid square S-9 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]],<ref name="Appendix" /> that was the [[homeworld]] of the [[Nikto]] [[species]], which was divided into at least three [[subspecies]]: the [[Color|green]]-skinned Nikto known as [[Kadas'sa'Nikto]],<ref name="Nikto (Red)" /> the lavender-skinned [[Esral'sa'Nikto]],<ref name="Oplock">{{Databank|oplock|Oplock}}</ref> and the red-skinned [[Kajain'sa'Nikto]].<ref name="Nikto (Red)" /> It was conquered by the [[Hutt Clan|Hutt Cartel]], which was controlled by the [[Hutt]]s from the neighboring world of [[Nal Hutta]], who turned the Nikto into [[Slavery|slaves]] or vassals.<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" /> [[Klaatu]], a [[Gender|male]] Kadas'sa'Nikto [[Gambling|gambler]] who worked as a henchman for the [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]], was from this world.<ref name="Klaatu">{{Databank|klaatu|Klaatu}}</ref> Creatures known as [[Kintan strider]]s, whose appearance was used as a piece in the game [[dejarik]], were from this world.<ref name="AEYNTK" /><ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> Kintan was the homeworld of the [[Kintan Striders Gang]].<ref name="Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref>

The Nikto [[Nenavakasa Nalor]]<ref name="The Engineer" /> hailed from Kintan and<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> [[Standard year|years]] before<ref name="The Engineer" /> [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{ResistanceDate|2|5}}</ref> was enslaved by [[pirate]]s. The pirates later sold Nalor to a [[Unidentified Hutt clan|Hutt clan]], who enslaved her for years until the Nikto<ref name="The Engineer" /> bravely<ref name="Databank" /> escaped from the clan and eventually left her homeworld.<ref name="The Engineer" />

In 34 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]],<ref name="Date" /> Nalor was hired by the [[First Order]] to [[Sabotage of the Colossus|sabotage]] the ''[[Colossus]]'' [[Supertanker fuel depot|refueling station]]. In order to board the [[Space station|station]], Nalor sent out a [[distress signal]] from her [[Nena's ship|starship]], claiming the First Order had attacked her. When two residents of the station&mdash;[[Kazuda Xiono]] and [[Synara San]]&mdash;investigated the signal, the Nikto lied to them by informing them she had barely escaped from her world after the attack, which had resulted in damage to her [[Starship|ship]]. Afterward, she accompanied the two back to the ''Colossus''. While aboard the station, Nalor deceived the ''Colossus'' resident [[Neeku Vozo]] into helping her [[Saboteur|sabotage]] the station. As the two worked together, she disclosed to him about her enslavement as a child. Once San and Xiono uncovered her deception, Nalor fled the ''Colossus'', though not before informing Vozo she had not lied to him about her childhood.<ref name="The Engineer" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Kintan.jpg|thumb|right|224px|Kintan as depicted in ''Star wars'' Legends.]]
Kintan was first mentioned in ''[[Galaxy Guide 12: Aliens — Enemies and Allies]]'', a [[1995]] [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] supplement for ''[[Star Wars: The Roleplaying Game]]''.<ref name="Aliens — Enemies and Allies">''[[Galaxy Guide 12: Aliens — Enemies and Allies]]''</ref> It became [[canon]] when it was mentioned in ''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]'', a reference book co-written by [[Tricia Barr|Patricia Barr]], [[Adam Bray]], [[Daniel Wallace]], and [[Ryder Windham]]<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> that was released on [[April 28]], [[2015]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars release date">{{DK|url=us/book/9781465436016-ultimate-star-wars|text=Ultimate Star Wars|nolive=1}}</ref>

